{"title":"Mock AIME 1 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Modified_Problem\">Modified Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Modified Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Prime_number\" title=\"Prime number\">prime number</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, define the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Function\" title=\"Function\">function</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e69816c2f00ee4d53fc3e1756cc926ec0ce264.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_p(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" /> as follows:\nIf there exists <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/0/6708ac84710a11cd355df3230653f3866524c596.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq y &lt; p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" />, such that \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/4/914b0be649d44a937d301388611a94ef240aed9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ny-p\\left\\lfloor \\frac{ny}{p}\\right\\rfloor=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"132\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/b/33bd64acd94b104a5d517e9cc867a62bce74e093.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_p(n) = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" />.  Otherwise, set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/6/236410b91875590da7c4584bf7b395eab436f2b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_p(n) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />.  Compute the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/e/71e5ab1a7ffcf6dfbebf7c6cfcbbf426db44187e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{11}(1) + f_{11}(2) + \\ldots + f_{11}(120) + f_{11}(121)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"329\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Original_Problem\">Original Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Original Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be a prime and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/c/75c5802fb0edc891b81590853f2dc7a498bf45be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le f(n) &lt;p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" /> for all <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integers</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/1/441416e660d25335f27e55334ac2a06e51541c97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Floor_function\" title=\"Floor function\"> greatest integer less than or equal to</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. If for fixed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, there exists an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/b/40b90aa84595ab161e3691f8d6f4420a74309edf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le y &lt; p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" /> such that:\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/4/914b0be649d44a937d301388611a94ef240aed9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ny-p\\left\\lfloor \\frac{ny}{p}\\right\\rfloor=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"132\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><br />\nthen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/4/fe4ff7f3a033a357ab7ed2f21daeb8a8a9388676.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />. If there is no such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63ca62369ad0c0587639f57d93a243816307b960.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/b/5eb5a1402e5a2040d6bf90ffcbcdf8a62633c8d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />, find the sum: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/2/b62a89e78c0288b7f467f2c547a508a71f789834.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)+f(2)+...+f(p^{2}-1)+f(p^{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"285\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The definition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/f/19f7e4e386aa055088d01c490e46b7586c1e9f76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"15\" height=\"17\" /> is equivalent to the following:  \"If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> has a multiplicative <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Inverse_with_respect_to_an_operation\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Inverse with respect to an operation\"> inverse</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mod&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mod (page does not exist)\">mod</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e69816c2f00ee4d53fc3e1756cc926ec0ce264.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_p(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" /> is the member of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Set\" title=\"Set\">set</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/9/39984ba9e36631548631accfdb986095e026bdf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{0, 1, \\ldots, p - 1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/6/9d66390f05561c771369b82bebef33d59845568e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\cdot f_p(n) \\equiv 1 \\pmod p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"169\" height=\"18\" />.  Otherwise, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/6/236410b91875590da7c4584bf7b395eab436f2b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_p(n) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />.\"  \n</p><p>Note that this really gives a well-defined function because that set includes exactly one member from each <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Congruence_class&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Congruence class (page does not exist)\">congruence class</a> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and each invertible element has inverses in only one such class.\n</p><p>From this point onwards, it's clear: as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> cycles through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/b/aabd5945302a15c1a287238954f78246de3486a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, \\ldots, 10 \\pmod{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"168\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e69816c2f00ee4d53fc3e1756cc926ec0ce264.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_p(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" /> also cycles through the same values in some order.  We cover those values 11 times.  Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/e/feeb97cfb011201830c7178c9eaaf4a0dfda5c0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 \\cdot (1 + 2 + \\ldots + 10) = 605$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"220\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 4\"> Previous Problem</a></li></ul>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 6\"> Next Problem</a></li></ul>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2006-2007\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2006-2007\">Mock AIME 1 2006-2007</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018035545\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.037 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 158/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6227/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3506:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018035545 and revision id 45997. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}